    <item>
      <title>Dependency alert: browser-use 1.0.2 pins pydantic-ai-slim==2.66.0 while pydantic-ai 2.67 demands 2.67.0 - the two will not install in the same environment</title>
      <link>https://www.aiagentsinfo.com/blog/ai-agent-framework-release-november-2026</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.aiagentsinfo.com/blog/ai-agent-framework-release-november-2026</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0800</pubDate>
      <category>AI &amp; Agents</category>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://www.aiagentsinfo.com/opengraph-image?v=e2c823d5" alt="AI Agents Info headline card for the browser-use / Pydantic AI pin conflict" style="max-width:100%"/></p>
<p><b>pydantic-ai 2.67 adds instruction files, durable sub-agents and operator authority; browser-use 1.0's persistent-REPL-on-CDP rewrite rides on it. AG2 1.3.1 and FastMCP 4.1.8 shipped in the same 48-hour window.</b></p>
<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.aiagentsinfo.com/blog/ai-agent-framework-release-november-2026">AI Agents Info</a></p>
<p>Feedback: <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/11%3A%20loved%20%22Dependency%20alert%3A%20browser-use%201.0.2%20pin...%22">Loved it</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/11%3A%20meh%20on%20%22Dependency%20alert%3A%20browser-use%201.0.2%20pin...%22">Meh</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/11%3A%20less%20like%20%22Dependency%20alert%3A%20browser-use%201.0.2%20pin...%22">Less of this</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=https%3A//www.aiagentsinfo.com/blog/ai-agent-framework-release-november-2026%0A">Chat about it</a></p>]]></description>
