      <title>An Alaska Airlines pilot aborted her SFO landing Tuesday after spotting another plane crossing the runway - FAA and NTSB scrutiny expected</title>
      <link>https://www.nbcbayarea.com/news/local/alaska-airlines-flight-aborts-landing-sfo-runway/4174019/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nbcbayarea.com/news/local/alaska-airlines-flight-aborts-landing-sfo-runway/4174019/</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:15:00 -0800</pubDate>
      <category>San Francisco</category>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://media.nbcbayarea.com/2026/11/Alaska-Airlines-flight-forced-to-abort-landing-at-SFO-after-another-aircraft-spotted-on-runway.jpg?quality=85&amp;strip=all&amp;resize=1200%2C675" alt="Alaska Airlines plane at SFO" style="max-width:100%"/></p>
<p><b>Flight 528's go-around drew comparisons to Air Canada's 2017 taxiway near-miss at SFO. Per FAA data, go-arounds happen in 1 to 3 of every 1,000 flights; SFO's parallel runways handle over 1,000 flights a day.</b></p>
<blockquote>&ldquo;We thought the best course of action was the safest one, and we'll come back around and do it again.&rdquo; - <a href="https://www.nbcbayarea.com/news/local/alaska-airlines-flight-aborts-landing-sfo-runway/4174019/">Alaska Flight 528 pilot, over the cabin intercom</a></blockquote>
